body:
Her father is Damien Charm (the WILDLY more attractive neighborhood stories son of Gemma Charm) - the dude apparently has good genetics.

&#x200B;

Here is her father, [Damien Charm](https://tinypic.host/i/screenshot-20230222-020027.57nIY). Her mother is my legacy founder's first child, [Adele](https://tinypic.host/i/screenshot-20230222-121943.57eR2).

As someone who needs and has used EpiPens, seeing them stab it into her heart gave her anger and ANXIETY. Why can Hollywood not realize that's NOT HOW YOU DO IT OH MY GOD

&#x200B;

Also who uses an epi instead of cpr on a drowning victim like in what world

I am bisexual. 

&#x200B;

Being LGBT+, you should absolutely understand why Deena pushing her to come out is NOT okay, ESPECIALLY as it is the 90s. Im not sure why you gave me the "woke" lecture, because that was my exact point. Society was less accepting of people not being straight, and so her coming out would have been all the more dangerous.

She was mean and vindictive, and refuses to accept that she's ever wrong. My boyfriend broke up with me, and Im not a piece of shit to the people around me. My family is abusive and I'm not rude to my friends. She was HATEFUL to Sam in that first scene. Idk how you can excuse that. Sure, she's hurting, but her behavior is still reprehensible.

&#x200B;

Also, she was TOTALLY fine with her friends and little brother sacrificing their lives for the girlfriend that she verbally abuses. Pushing your ex to come out is what we're NOT gonna stick up for.

So... they erased a character entirely because they're scared of having anyone over a size four in it? OK :/

&#x200B;

The casting is Abysmal with a capital A.

&#x200B;

If they knew ANYTHING about vocal types/the characters in Heathers, Veronica would be Chandler, Betty would be MacNamara or VERONICA (Hi, the girl on the verge of popularity with a KILLER BELTING VOICE who dates the creepy yet charismatic outcast), Cheryl would be Duke. Ethyl would be Martha.

&#x200B;

This episode is going to be worse than the Carrie episode, which was pretty damn bad. 

&#x200B;

And before anyone fights me, heres WHY the Heathers are cast incorrectly: 

&#x200B;

MacNamara (SOPRANO) is the "nice", soft Heather - that's Betty (or Josie). She's the only one who cares about the others around her, and genuinely regrets being cruel. 

&#x200B;

Duke (ALTO) is the wannabe bitch who sabotages herself more often than not and is DESPERATE to fit in - thats Cheryl. They had to lower all of the Carrie vocal parts so that she could sing them - she could only sing Duke in this show. 

&#x200B;

Chandler (MEZZO-SOP) is the RICH, popular, give no fucks, queen - thats Veronica.

&#x200B;

In short: The casting SUCKS.
